WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.601
Actress Michelle Yeoh

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.770
is no fan of glass ceilings.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.872
Neither her age nor her nationality,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.741
nor her gender can stop her

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.776
from taking Hollywood by storm

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.145
Fresh off a Golden Globe award

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.947
for her virtuoso performance

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.216
in Everything, Everywhere All At Once,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.417
Yellow leads

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.486
the list of contenders for this year's

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.454
best actress Oscar.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:21.988
Her star

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.324
vehicle is an idiosyncratic movie

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:26.493
about a Chinese laundromat owner

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.161
thrust into a mission

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.630
to save all possible universes.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.432
So no pressure there.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.600
Take a look at this clip

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.701
from the trailer.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.137
He's waiting in the wings.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.071
The universe

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.873
he speaks of senseless

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.610
things is so much bigger

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.178
than you realize.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:50.784
From all the places

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.851
I could be

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.922
I just want to pursue this.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.322
You

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.192
remember our mission

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.060
transcending the fate

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.960
of every single will

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.262
of our infinite multiverse.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.267
There is no way I am the Evelyn

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.268
you are looking for.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.036
And Michelle Yeoh is with me here.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.304
Welcome to the program.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.372
Thank you so much.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.573
I'm so happy to be here.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.075
Well, it is amazing.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.709
And you've got so many accolades

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.578
for this remarkable role.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.713
What I just literally can't believe

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:21.781
and I wonder how you feel about

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.850
it is the first Hollywood movie

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.119
where you have had top billing in a long

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.487
and distinguished career.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.755
When you saw the script

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.589
and you saw your role,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.857
what did you think?

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.860
First of all, I prayed and say, please

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.628
let these two boys

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.198
not be certifiably insane, okay?

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:41.501
The two boys are the Daniels who wrote

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.670
this is the original screenplay.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.571
It's come from Daniel

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.639
Kwan and Daniel Shine.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.075
And when I received it, you know,

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.678
it's like you received scripts and as

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.114
the years get

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.849
bigger, the numbers get bigger.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.584
The roles seem to shrink

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.651
with that, right.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.220
As you know, as a woman,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.522
as an aging woman or whatever it is,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.791
somehow they start putting you in boxes.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:05.825
And it's always

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.161
the guy who gets to go on the adventure

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.863
and save the world

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.397
and, you know, rescue your daughter.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.900
And you think, why can't I do that, too?

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.704
So it was so overwhelming

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.006
at that point to get a script

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.141
that said you know,

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.611
this is a very ordinary woman, an Asian

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.712
immigrant woman

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.914
who's dealing with all the problems

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.350
that we all can relate to while

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.418
maybe not as a laundromat owner, but,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.120
you know, the relationship

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.588
with your husband, relationship

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.090
with your father, relationship

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.857
with your daughter

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.293
I mean, that's the generational gap

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.929
that miscommunication between

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.998
mothers and daughters especially.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.267
It's always been more complicated.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.836
And what I loved about it, it was like

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.005
this is an ordinary woman

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.773
who is being seen,

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:54.941
who is given a role

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.076
to play as a superhero.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.811
And that's what we are

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.880
women mothers, daughters,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.582
sisters are superheroes

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.851
because we have a certain superpower,

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.054
which is kindness, love, compassion

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:12.091
and the core of this crazy, wacky, messy,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.595
you know, frenetic story on the surface.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.566
The core is authentic, genuine, love,

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.967
full family

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.336
and never giving up on each other.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.971
I am going to play a clip

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.106
where you don't look for love

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.875
and compassion. Who are you?

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.544
Very, very out.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.378
Let's say this.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.515
Let's play this clip from

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.023
Go

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.539
Oh, look,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.495
ow, ow, ow,

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.697
ow, ow.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:29.502
Look

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.437
what happened.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.374
I think they lost their powers

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.278
So in this, a madcap sci

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.447
fi and multi genre film, at least

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.216
you would want to list the genres,

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.018
because it is it is crazy.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.618
It is.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.186
Sci fi is horror,

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:50.456
it's romance, it's drama, it's comedy.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:51.791
It's like

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.259
maybe I've been in rehearsing

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:56.262
for 40 years for this ultimate role.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:05:00.233
It is just amazing to be able to have

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:03.303
the opportunity to say, I can do this.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.705
Please let me show you.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.173
And you have done

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.375
what is the compassionate mother that

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.145
she was doing acting.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.314
Her daughter and the husband

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.215
because these

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.884
I don't know what you call them,

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.252
the agents have come

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.720
from another universe

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.622
and they are trying to destroy

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.957
each universe system magically.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.160
So what we have to do is to try it.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:27.960
I have to do

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.630
is to protect my universe, my family.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.566
And this is backwards.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.834
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.036
And this is the multi universe thing

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.971
that is, you know, is the.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.639
It's amazing

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:40.340
because what

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.808
the Daniels have done is like,

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:44.043
you know, how we look at our lives

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:44.911
and we look

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:45.812
and we say,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:48.014
I wish I had done it differently.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.582
Perhaps the outcome

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.351
would have been better.

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.552
And you know how

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.654
especially immigrant parents

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.756
have a tendency to say to their children,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.692
I left a good life for you

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.161
so you can have a better life?

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.696
I could have done things differently,

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.098
but for you.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.099
So sometimes it's

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:08.368
that miscommunication into feeling.

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.036
And then the younger ones go like,

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.204
you don't have to do things for me.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.572
I could do it for myself.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.374
So I see what this movie,

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.642
when it came out, it appealed.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.812
It resonated with different generations.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.848
It was like shining a light on them

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:22.348
to say

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.450
sometimes we just have to step back.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.519
The motivation is really from love

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:27.987
is from care.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.189
And what I really love is

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.158
sometimes people walk up to the streets

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.159
and say,

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:35.061
I'm about my age and say,

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.529
I didn't really get your movie

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:37.163
because, you know,

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.098
it gets a little crazy for me.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.400
But I was confused, too.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:40.967
Yeah,

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:43.703
but my estranged young daughter

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:45.872
that I have not spoken to in the movie.

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:46.472
No, no.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.907
In real life

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.709
came to the mother and say,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.277
I've watched this movie.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:52.512
And I think I understand

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:54.814
what you are trying to do for me.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.917
So it's healed certain relationships,

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:00.253
it's opened up conversations,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.687
and I think that's what we need to do.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:02.955
Is have conversations

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.590
because the last few years

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.261
have been so difficult on so many levels.

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:08.995
Right?

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.631
With the pandemic, with with things

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.833
with tragedies and things like that,

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.635
it was nice to have a movie

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.636
where it's like

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.772
embraced here.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:20.873
How does it

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:23.443
how does some of this play into

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.178
or play off your own experience?

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:27.480
You also are an immigrant,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.282
you know, from Malaysia.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:30.817
But nonetheless,

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:33.152
you left in order to have a better life.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.688
You came from a very, you know,

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.590
I guess, upper middle class family.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.659
The father was a lawyer.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.294
How does that

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.496
does any part of your experience resonate

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:45.031
with the film character?

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.999
It resonated tremendously.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:49.035
I think what it resonated with

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.870
was the relationship

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.372
you know, with the older generation

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:54.841
understanding.

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:55.575
I have,

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:56.876
unfortunately, you know,

00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:58.377
too many conversations.

00:07:58.377 --> 00:08:00.313
Luckily, not from my parents,

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.981
where my father was very forward

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.349
thinking, was never,

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.884
never told any of us

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:07.653
that, you know, daughters were

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:09.989
next behind the son.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:10.923
So in that way,

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.992
he empowered me to believe

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.093
that, you know,

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:15.328
if you believe you can do

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.796
it, you should go for it.

00:08:16.796 --> 00:08:18.731
And that was how it always has been

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:21.033
with myself, my career in that way.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.002
So I felt it was very important

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:23.569
to shine

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:24.637
the light of someone

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.739
who didn't have that kind of privilege,

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.875
who didn't have that kind of support.

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.943
Like Evelyn Wong her father.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.011
That's you in the film.

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.179
That's me in the film.

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:34.480
Literally just said to you

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.115
your complete failure rate.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:38.284
I tell you not to go off with this man.

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:39.652
Look where you end up

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.153
in a failing laundromat.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.055
Bad business with a daughter

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.891
that looks like a mess.

00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:46.359
But I think at the end of the day,

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:47.860
it was like I remember,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:48.528
I think

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:49.128
at that time

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.429
when my dad said to me,

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:53.366
I wish you enough, I didn't quite get it.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.801
But I think with this movie,

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.336
what resonated was

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:58.271
she told her daughter,

00:08:58.271 --> 00:08:59.805
it doesn't matter what you are,

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:01.040
how you think.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.643
You're not living up to my expectations.

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:04.977
You are enough.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.414
You and just about everybody

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:09.382
to do with this film

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.450
have been nominated in

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.253
in all your categories.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:15.888
I was just staggered to read

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.223
that actually, Jackie Chan

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.125
might have been chosen for the lead

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.360
role, that it might have gone to a man

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.129
and somebody much older than you.

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:25.331
Obviously, it was written for man.

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:26.365
When Daniel

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.000
set out to do this, you know,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.303
I think whenever filmmakers

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:30.970
tell the story,

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.538
they also have to be mindful

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.073
it is show business.

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:35.241
I have to write something

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:37.777
that somebody will make it into a film

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:39.812
and so they wrote it

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:41.447
like that way with Jackie

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:43.215
and me as the wife.

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:44.717
So it was completely

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:45.918
the role was reversed.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:46.552
Yeah.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:47.687
And I remember

00:09:47.687 --> 00:09:48.521
Jackie texted me

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:49.789
and said, congratulations.

00:09:49.789 --> 00:09:50.056
You know,

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:50.590
you realize

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.224
that your boys came to see me first,

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:54.026
and I'm like, Thank you, bro.

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:55.761
I mean, seriously, a huge favor.

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:56.162
Yeah.

00:09:56.896 --> 00:09:58.531
So did you turn it down

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:00.166
or did the Daniels decide that?

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:01.133
I think it was

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.536
it was it was mutual because, you know,

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:05.371
Jackie is very, very busy.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:05.805
And, you know,

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:07.840
he's got so many things going on.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:08.641
And I think

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.843
Daniels also stepped back and said,

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.144
then we're doing something

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:14.180
that's already been done before

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:17.149
why we should do it differently.

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:20.186
And they both have very strong women

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:23.122
in their lives, whether it's the mothers

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:26.392
or the the wife and the partners.

00:10:26.392 --> 00:10:28.461
So they are very inspired

00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:31.230
and they're not afraid of strong women.

00:10:31.497 --> 00:10:33.366
I think that is the most beautiful thing

00:10:33.366 --> 00:10:35.167
about these boys, just like

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.136
they celebrate strong woman.

